I think I'm having an issue where a css and a js asset are siblings (js file `require`d the css, [this test](https://github.com/parcel-bundler/parcel/tree/master/packages/core/integration-tests/test/integration/html-css-optional-elements)) and both add their sourcemap to a sibling sourcemap bundle (of which there can only be one?).
> Perhaps in Bundle#addAsset we could add the map to a sibling map bundle? 

```js
Bundle {
	type: "html"
	childBundles: [
		Bundle {
			type: "js"
			entryAsset: JSAsset
			assets: [
				JSAsset {},
				CSSAsset {}
			],
			childBundles: [
				Bundle {type: "map" /* .js.map */ }
				Bundle {
					type: "css"
					childBundles: {
						{type: "map" /* .css.map */}
					},
					siblingBundles: /* same as childBundles*/
				}
			]
			siblingBundles: /* same as childBundles*/
		}
	],
	siblingBundles: [/* empty */]
}
```
result: `.js.map` contains the mappings for CSS as well.

